+# Changes · Piece 2 (Header)
+
+## What changed
+
+- `src/format.mjs` (new): `formatValue(value, unit)` (usd -> `$1.42M`, count -> `38.2k`,
+  cents -> `$37.24`, derived from `unit`), `formatPercent(delta)` (absolute, one
+  decimal), `escapeXml`.
+- `src/header.mjs`: rewritten on the shared geometry from `src/layout.mjs` (not changed).
+  - Title at (32, 54), 20px semi-bold `#111827`; period at (32, 74), 12px `#6b7280`.
+  - Three tiles at y=90, 184 x 80, rx 8, fill `#f3f4f6`, gap 12: the row runs from
+    x=32 to x=608 exactly (the margins).
+  - Fixed baselines in every tile (offsets 24 / 54 / 70 from the tile top), text inset 14:
+    upper-case label (10px, 600, muted), value (28px, 700, dark), change line (11px, 600).
+  - Change line: `▲`/`▼`, absolute percent to one decimal, "vs prior period", in one
+    green (`#15803d`) for a rise and one red (`#b91c1c`) for a fall; everything else is grey.
+- `tests/card.test.mjs`: the label check is now case-insensitive; added a check that
+  every compact value, percentage and both marks appear. Nothing removed or weakened.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+All points met. `npm test` passes (5 tests); `npm run capture` written; the frame element is
+unchanged and first. `src/trend.mjs` and `src/card.mjs` untouched.
+
+## Left on purpose
+
+- The change line is one `<text>` (whole line in the sign colour) rather than a coloured
+  mark plus grey phrase, because the capture script does not list nested `<tspan>` text.
+- The trend bars are still the old placeholder (black, 10px offset): Piece 3's scope.
